{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Therefore \"upon you\"</b> — concerning the heavens, like <i>\"and your heavens that are over your head [shall be bronze]\"</i>, or \"upon you\" alone — not upon the inhabitants of the earth." "<b>He withheld</b> — the word [means] the dew."], :book :haggai, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Cross-reference to Deuteronomy 28:23.", 1 "Reading מלתת as מְלַת־תַּת, 'the word [meaning] giving/withholding'; the form is unusual and possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Haggai" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"] ["Ibn Ezra on Haggai -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/hagai"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:49:22.253533738Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}